---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-ai-summary</code> is a summary the assistant wrote: the day's items on Home, a long thread,
  the answer to an administrator's question. The facts come from the platform; the summary puts them
  into words, cites the records, and is marked as the assistant's (ADR-030002).
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-ai-summary
    id='summary-demo'
    headline='For you today'
    badge-label='Summary by the assistant'
    style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 36rem;'
    value={'- Your leave on 13 November is still waiting for Ada Lovelace[1](cite:lv_7). You asked 6 days ago.\n- 3 of your tasks in Website relaunch are due this week; one was due yesterday[2](cite:pr_12).'}
  >
    <wc-link slot='why' href='#'>Why these items?</wc-link>
  </wc-ai-summary>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var el = document.querySelector('#summary-demo');
      el.citations = [
        { id: 'lv_7', headline: 'Leave request · 13 November', supportingText: 'Human resources' },
        { id: 'pr_12', headline: 'Update the pricing page copy', supportingText: 'Projects · Website relaunch' },
      ];
      var full = el.value;
      el.addEventListener('regenerate', function () {
        el.loading = true;
        el.status = 'Checking your apps…';
        setTimeout(function () {
          el.loading = false;
          el.streaming = true;
          var shown = 0;
          var timer = setInterval(function () {
            shown = Math.min(full.length, shown + 5);
            el.value = full.slice(0, shown);
            if (shown >= full.length) {
              clearInterval(timer);
              el.streaming = false;
            }
          }, 40);
        }, 1200);
      });
      el.addEventListener('dismiss', function () {
        myConsole.log('dismiss: hide it for today');
        el.hidden = true;
        setTimeout(function () {
          el.hidden = false;
        }, 1500);
      });
      el.addEventListener('feedback', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('feedback: ' + (event.detail.value || 'none'));
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>States</h3>
<p>
  <code>loading</code> shows placeholder lines and <code>status</code> while the summary is prepared;
  <code>streaming</code> grows the text with a caret; <code>error</code> says it couldn't be written and
  offers Try again, leaving whatever it sits on unaffected. Press Try again in the demo above.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: grid; gap: 1rem; inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 36rem;'>
    <wc-ai-summary headline='Thread summary' loading status='Reading 14 comments…'></wc-ai-summary>
    <wc-ai-summary headline='Thread summary' error></wc-ai-summary>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Inline insight</h3>
<p>
  <code>variant="inline"</code> is a single line with a sparkle, for the <code>insight</code> slot of
  <code>wc-stat</code> and the charts. The number comes from the platform; the insight only explains it.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-stat label='Open incidents' value='42' previous='31' variant='outlined' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 22rem;'>
    <wc-ai-summary slot='insight' variant='inline' value='Up 35% since Monday: 9 of the 11 new ones are the export failure.'></wc-ai-summary>
  </wc-stat>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>When AI is off</h3>
<p>
  The summary renders nothing, so the page under it must make sense without it: Home still shows the
  app tiles, the thread still shows every comment.
</p>
